{"id": "EUVD-2026-99253", "enisaUuid": "c40a3cdd-6f62-3292-98a8-0430c095bbdc", "description": "Stonewuu ai-fusion-video through 1.2.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows authenticated users to write uploaded files outside the media directory via the subDir parameter of POST /api/storage/upload. Attackers can supply parent-directory sequences that LocalStorageStrategy.storeBytes never normalizes, creating directories and writing attacker-controlled files with chosen extensions anywhere the service account can write.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:18:53", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/ai-fusion-video-broken-access-control-and-upload-path-traversal", "https://github.com/Stonewuu/ai-fusion-video/blob/v1.2.0/ai-fusion-video/src/main/java/com/stonewu/fusion/service/storage/strategy/LocalStorageStrategy.java#L77-L92", "https://github.com/Stonewuu/ai-fusion-video/blob/v1.2.0/ai-fusion-video/src/main/java/com/stonewu/fusion/controller/storage/FileUploadController.java#L72-L99", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ai-fusion-video-through-1.2.0-path-traversal-in-media-upload-subdir-parameter"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110212", "GHSA-56g6-3cr7-7xx2"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3e9e8a24-aa68-37f8-8959-d99f81385a81", "product": {"name": "ai-fusion-video", "vendor": {"name": "Stonewuu"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2e0c6bbb-137a-3e27-adf0-ef3ea7f6ae33", "vendor": {"name": "Stonewuu"}}], "isExploited": false}